  "solution": "Given:\n\nx(5-(2)/(x))= (5)/(x) \n\nFormula used:\n\n(a + b)2 = a2 + 2ab + b2\n\n(a + b)3 = a3 + 3ab(a + b) + b3\n\nCalculation:\n\nx(5-(2)/(x))= (5)/(x) \n\n⇒ 5x - 2 = (5)/(x) \n\n⇒ 5x - (5)/(x) = 2\n\n⇒ 5(x - 1/x) = 2\n\n⇒ (x - 1/x) = 2/5\n\nSquaring both sides\n\n⇒ x² + 1/x² - 2 = 4/25\n\n⇒ x2 + 1/x2 = 4/25 + 2\n\n⇒ x2 + 1/x2 = 54/25\n\n**∴ Option 1 is the correct answer.**\n\nx(5-(2)/(x))= (5)/(x)",
